@startuml
title UC-13/14 - Detect, Evaluate and Block Website (FST-050 design boundary)
autonumber
participant "Website integration\n(mechanism not selected)" as Integration
participant "WebsiteObservationPort" as Observation
participant "Website detection use case" as Detect
participant "Session / policy reader" as Current
participant "DistractionPolicyService + BlockingPolicy" as Policy
participant "Transactional outbox" as Outbox
participant "WebsiteBlockerPort" as Blocker
participant "Outbox dispatcher" as Dispatch
participant "Log projection / WebSocket" as Consumers

note over Integration, Blocker
  Planned contract only. FST-050 must agree browser/OS support,
  mechanism, permissions, local transport and cleanup guarantees.
  A window title is not proof of the website host.
end note
Integration -> Observation : website observation trigger
Observation -> Detect : request observation handling
Detect -> Current : current state and active policy
Current --> Detect : session, interval, policy
alt RUNNING + WORK and supported observation capability
  Detect -> Observation : read actual host and transient context
  Observation -> Integration : obtain host for current page/request
  Integration --> Observation : host + transient context
  Observation --> Detect : host + transient context
  Detect -> Policy : evaluate normalized host
  note right of Policy
    youtube.com matches youtube.com and music.youtube.com.
    Does not match notyoutube.com or youtube.com.example.org.
    Most specific matching domain wins; disabled rules ignored.
  end note
  Policy --> Detect : decision or no match
  alt enabled website rule matches
    Detect -> Outbox : append DistractionDetected\n(detectionId, rule/host snapshot, action)
    Detect -> Outbox : commit detection transaction
    alt BLOCK
      Detect -> Current : recheck session, rule and host context
      Current --> Detect : eligible / stale
      alt still eligible
        Detect -> Blocker : restrict matched site/context
        Blocker -> Integration : apply site-specific protection
        Integration --> Blocker : confirmed or failure with reason
        Blocker --> Detect : outcome
        Detect -> Outbox : append DistractionBlocked or\nDistractionBlockFailed (same detectionId)
        Detect -> Outbox : commit outcome transaction
      else stale
        note right of Detect : Cancel; do not report successful blocking.
      end
    else WARN
      Detect -> Consumers : request local warning
    else LOG
      note right of Detect : Record detection only.
    end
    Dispatch -> Outbox : read committed detection/outcome events
    Outbox --> Dispatch : events (delivery may be out of order)
    Dispatch -> Consumers : correlate/deduplicate, project and notify
  else no match
    note right of Detect : No session detection or block.
  end
else inactive focus / unavailable capability
  note right of Detect
    No website collection or enforcement.
    Report missing capability; keep timer working.
  end note
end
note over Integration, Blocker
  A site rule must not terminate the entire browser.
  Retain host identity, not URL credentials/query or page content.
  Release introduced restrictions when focus eligibility ends.
end note
@enduml
